{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793181513,"nonce":"EqUaIl4IntxvHgGx9p/7IJJZzpE=","message":"The Pocket Studio template and existing managed demo now ignore .rayde/. Browser sample packaging excludes .rayde/ as well as .rayzor/, dependencies and artifacts.\n\nAdded an explicit --prepare-only operator command. It uses Rayzor itself with the same default 5000 ms macro budget, canonical persistent workspace and session environment, then verifies reuse in a second fresh LSP process. Normal app startup, serving, page load and refresh never invoke preparation. No frontend semantic cache or runtime prewarming wait was added.\n\nActual persistent demo: Main.hx and BoardApp.hx both reused their existing disk indexes in the preparation and fresh-process verification (2 reused, 0 indexed in each run). A real-LSP regression test proves cold indexing, new-process reuse without rewriting the index, and invalidation after a source edit. A stalled-process test verifies timeout cleanup. WASM and the native session were rebuilt; tested assets staged to bin/web/rayde. The existing services were left running.\n\nAn exploratory all-source preparation reached seven persisted indexes before its bounded 180-second timeout. Initial landing tabs are verified warm; broad cold indexing of other Ashui-heavy source tabs remains a separate performance concern and is not put on the startup path.","files":null}]}